.TH BSPWMCTL 1 "2026-10-29" "bspwmctl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bspwmctl \- opinionated bspwm desktop installer and manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bspwmctl
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bspwmctl
installs a complete bspwm desktop (bspwm, sxhkd, kitty, rofi, and optionally
polybar, picom, dunst, zsh and more) from the official packages of Debian,
Ubuntu, Arch, Fedora and their derivatives, and applies a ready-to-use
configuration to
.IR ~/.config .
.PP
Run every command as your normal user, not as root. bspwmctl uses
.BR sudo (8)
only to install packages and change the login shell.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
Install the packages for the selected mode and apply the configuration.
.TP
.B theme \fR[\fIname\fR]
Without a name, show the current theme and the available ones.
With a name, apply that theme. The only theme for now is
.BR default .
.TP
.B restore \fR[\fIbackup\fR]
Without arguments, list the config backups. With a backup name, restore it.
The current configs are backed up first, so a restore can be undone.
.TP
.B update \fR[\fB\-\-configs\fR]
Download the package of the latest release from GitHub and install it with
apt, dnf or pacman. Beta versions also update to newer betas; stable versions
only to stable releases. Only works when bspwmctl was installed as a package.
.TP
.B uninstall \fR[\fB\-y\fR]
Remove the configs, fonts and
.I ~/.zshrc
written by bspwmctl, restore the ones you had before and your previous login
shell. Everything removed is backed up first. Installed programs are kept.
.TP
.B help
Show the help panel.
.TP
.B version
Show the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS install
.TP
.B \-\-minimal
bspwm, sxhkd, kitty and rofi. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-standard
Also polybar, picom, dunst, a lock screen, screenshots, media keys and zsh,
which becomes the login shell.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Also a file manager, a browser and other applications.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dep
Don't install packages, only apply the configuration.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Theme to apply after installing (default:
.BR default ).
.SS update
.TP
.B \-\-configs
Also re-apply the configs of the current theme from the new version.
Your current configs are backed up first.
.SS uninstall
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Don't ask for confirmation.
.SS Global
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help panel.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bspwm, sxhkd, kitty, polybar, picom, dunst
Configs applied by bspwmctl.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bspwm/wallpaper.png \fRor\fP .jpg
Wallpaper, if present.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bspwmctl/backups/
Backups of the configs replaced by bspwmctl, one directory per run.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bspwmctl/
Also stores the current theme and what existed before bspwmctl, for
.BR uninstall .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/fonts/bspwmctl/
Bundled fonts.
.TP
.I /usr/share/bspwmctl/config/
Default configs shipped with the package.
.PP
.I ~/.local/share
is
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME
when it is set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error; the message explains why.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled with Ctrl+C.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B bspwmctl install \-\-standard
Install the recommended desktop.
.TP
.B bspwmctl theme default
Re-apply the default configs.
.TP
.B bspwmctl update \-\-configs
Update bspwmctl and apply its new configs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bspwm (1),
.BR bspc (1),
.BR sxhkd (1)
.PP
Documentation: https://bspwmctl.github.io/docs/
.br
Source and bug reports: https://github.com/bspwmctl/bspwmctl
